It can't be helped, I'm afraid.

511
00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:26.011
What can I say? It's all on me.

512
00:22:26.078 --> 00:22:29.281
Honestly, I feel like I let my team down.

513
00:22:29.348 --> 00:22:33.752
I don't think I did my job very well
as team captain.

514
00:22:48.434 --> 00:22:50.703
If we'd lost, we'd be in there with them.

515
00:22:51.904 --> 00:22:53.339
Seriously, man.

516
00:22:54.106 --> 00:22:55.674
This stings.

517
00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:57.276
Losing sucks, huh?

518
00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:00.713
Round 2 of <i>I Am Boxer</i> is over.

519
00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.816
Well done, fighters.

520
00:23:06.986 --> 00:23:09.989
As a result of Round 2,
the four winning teams,

521
00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:12.157
a total of 24 fighters,

522
00:23:12.758 --> 00:23:16.395
have survived and will advance
to the next round. Congratulations.

523
00:23:20.299 --> 00:23:22.568
As for the four losing teams,

524
00:23:22.635 --> 00:23:24.036
a total of 24 fighters,

525
00:23:24.703 --> 00:23:26.105
have been eliminated

526
00:23:26.639 --> 00:23:28.841
from <i>I Am Boxer</i>.

527
00:23:30.009 --> 00:23:31.243
Guess we're done here.

528
00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:33.612
I really felt the regret.

529
00:23:33.679 --> 00:23:35.881
Honestly, I just felt empty.

530
00:23:36.382 --> 00:23:37.549
Guess I'm going home.

531
00:23:39.084 --> 00:23:40.319
You all fought hard.

532
00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:42.388
But...

533
00:23:42.454 --> 00:23:43.455
But...

534
00:23:46.225 --> 00:23:48.060
You will be given one more chance.

535
00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:52.865
Are we having a fight?

536
00:23:53.666 --> 00:23:56.135
I might get another shot at this.

537
00:23:56.702 --> 00:23:59.772
This chance will not be given to everyone.

538
00:23:59.838 --> 00:24:01.640
Out of the 24 who were eliminated,

539
00:24:02.041 --> 00:24:03.943
those who get to fight the deathmatch...

540
00:24:04.944 --> 00:24:06.946
are only 12.

541
00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:11.150
Exactly half.

542
00:24:11.617 --> 00:24:14.420
So not everyone's getting this chance.

543
00:24:14.486 --> 00:24:16.555
This is too cruel.

544
00:24:22.294 --> 00:24:24.396
Man, how are we gonna do this? Don.

545
00:24:24.897 --> 00:24:26.765
The one I feel worst about letting go...

546
00:24:26.832 --> 00:24:28.767
That would be Kim Minuk.

547
00:24:28.834 --> 00:24:30.502
He is such a skilled fighter.

548
00:24:30.569 --> 00:24:33.205
His style is so explosive.
I really liked that.

549
00:24:33.272 --> 00:24:35.507
All those elite boxers teamed up

550
00:24:35.574 --> 00:24:37.810
- and got knocked out together.
- All in one go.

551
00:24:37.876 --> 00:24:38.911
That's true.

552
00:24:38.978 --> 00:24:40.679
We can't lose all of them now.

553
00:24:41.313 --> 00:24:43.048
I wish I could save all of them, but...

554
00:24:43.115 --> 00:24:44.483
You should decide then.

555
00:24:44.550 --> 00:24:46.585
No, don't say that. I'm just as lost.

556
00:24:46.652 --> 00:24:47.987
- Hey.
- I can't do this.

557
00:24:48.053 --> 00:24:50.055
Seriously, this is giving me a headache.

558
00:24:50.122 --> 00:24:52.324
Man, this is tough.

559
00:24:53.659 --> 00:24:56.295
All right then, let me explain

560
00:24:56.362 --> 00:24:58.931
how the deathmatch
on <i>I Am Boxer</i> will work.

561
00:24:59.498 --> 00:25:02.801
This deathmatch will be fought one-on-one.

562
00:25:05.504 --> 00:25:09.608
Each bout will be 2 rounds of 3 minutes.

563
00:25:10.409 --> 00:25:11.543
Two rounds of three minutes.

564
00:25:12.077 --> 00:25:14.646
Basically, six minutes
straight without a break.

565
00:25:14.713 --> 00:25:17.349
Those two rounds will decide your fate.

566
00:25:17.416 --> 00:25:20.285
Stamina is going to be a huge factor.

567
00:25:20.352 --> 00:25:22.354
There is never an easy day.

568
00:25:22.788 --> 00:25:25.758
If there is no winner
within the two rounds,

569
00:25:25.824 --> 00:25:31.930
{\an8}the decision will go to the three judges,
including Master Don Lee.

570
00:25:32.531 --> 00:25:34.199
Please let me go one more time.

571
00:25:34.266 --> 00:25:36.068
I've still got the stamina for the ring.

572
00:25:36.635 --> 00:25:37.636
I hope I get picked.

573
00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:39.972
We were thrown a lifeline.

574
00:25:40.039 --> 00:25:41.473
I just wanted to grab it.

575
00:25:42.041 --> 00:25:43.575
I really wanted it.

576
00:25:43.642 --> 00:25:45.411
I thought,
"Let's climb back up from here."

577
00:25:47.279 --> 00:25:49.648
{\an8}I've never seen a fight this up close.

578
00:25:49.715 --> 00:25:51.216
So who are the 12 going to be?

579
00:25:51.283 --> 00:25:53.285
They'll probably start calling names here.

580
00:25:53.352 --> 00:25:55.220
Then even if you're not on the list,

581
00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.855
you just have to wait till the end

582
00:25:56.922 --> 00:25:58.590
- without knowing.
- Sweating bullets.

583
00:25:58.657 --> 00:26:01.226
At least we lose half the competition.

584
00:26:02.828 --> 00:26:08.133
Let me announce the first
matchup of <i>I Am Boxer's</i> deathmatch

585
00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:09.735
right now.

586
00:26:11.603 --> 00:26:14.673
The pressure is on a whole different level
compared to the first day.

587
00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:16.809
This is how society works.

588
00:26:16.875 --> 00:26:18.143
Welcome to reality.

589
00:26:18.210 --> 00:26:21.613
The first fighter
to enter the deathmatch is...

590
00:26:21.680 --> 00:26:22.915
Please, let it be me.

591
00:26:22.981 --> 00:26:24.316
The suspense is killing me.

592
00:26:25.250 --> 00:26:26.251
Who will it be?

593
00:26:28.220 --> 00:26:29.822
Pyeon Yejun.

594
00:26:31.757 --> 00:26:33.492
Gotta give it to him, he's good.

595
00:26:33.959 --> 00:26:36.829
Didn't Pyeon Yejun
get pretty famous recently?

596
00:26:36.895 --> 00:26:40.532
His KO win has hit
11 million views. This is "Pyeonstar"!

597
00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:42.868
Pyeon Yejun!

598
00:26:43.569 --> 00:26:44.903
Here comes Pyeon Yejun!

599
00:26:44.970 --> 00:26:46.238
There's another kick.

600
00:26:46.305 --> 00:26:47.406
Now it's the punches.

601
00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:51.310
The MMA guys these days
are really good at boxing.

602
00:26:51.376 --> 00:26:53.812
The MMA guys' skills have shot up lately.

603
00:26:53.879 --> 00:26:55.013
Let's go, Pyeon Yejun!

604
00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:56.115
You got this!

605
00:26:56.181 --> 00:26:58.317
Wow, I couldn't believe I was called.

606
00:26:58.383 --> 00:27:00.853
I was like,
"I have to win this and move up."

607
00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:03.422
Who is he going up against?

608
00:27:03.489 --> 00:27:05.190
The guy who sat right behind him?

609
00:27:06.525 --> 00:27:07.893
I was confident I could take him,

610
00:27:07.960 --> 00:27:10.062
so I was hoping to get called.

611
00:27:10.596 --> 00:27:14.433
I'm curious how he'd do
against one of Cho Hyunjae's amateur guys.

612
00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:15.701
Wonder how that'd go.

613
00:27:16.802 --> 00:27:19.138
The fighter facing Pyeon Yejun is...

614
00:27:19.705 --> 00:27:22.274
All those elite boxers teamed up

615
00:27:22.341 --> 00:27:23.842
and got knocked out together.

616
00:27:23.909 --> 00:27:26.078
- That's true.
- It's such a waste.

617
00:27:26.145 --> 00:27:28.013
- Like Cho Hyunjae here.
- You're right.

618
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:29.515
Same goes for him.

619
00:27:29.581 --> 00:27:30.883
- Lee Chaehyun.
- Right.

620
00:27:30.949 --> 00:27:33.852
They're both great fighters.

621
00:27:33.919 --> 00:27:38.257
They're some of the fighters
I really wanted to see box.

622
00:27:38.991 --> 00:27:41.393
The fighter facing Pyeon Yejun is...

623
00:27:44.396 --> 00:27:45.664
Cho Hyunjae.

624
00:27:45.731 --> 00:27:48.233
This is gonna be fun.

625
00:27:51.703 --> 00:27:52.838
I was happy,

626
00:27:52.905 --> 00:27:55.774
but with all my teammates
sitting in the elimination zone,

627
00:27:55.841 --> 00:27:57.543
I couldn't be all that happy.

628
00:27:58.310 --> 00:28:00.212
- Remember, it's two rounds.
- Let's go, cap!

629
00:28:00.279 --> 00:28:01.313
- Stay calm.
- You got this.

630
00:28:01.380 --> 00:28:02.381
Stay focused.

631
00:28:02.447 --> 00:28:03.949
Give it everything you got, man.

632
00:28:04.016 --> 00:28:06.818
- This should be fun.
- Who's gonna win?

633
00:28:07.986 --> 00:28:09.688
I'm ready to go do-or-die out here.

634
00:28:10.422 --> 00:28:13.458
I'm afraid I'll have to crush him
and move up.

635
00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:21.667
Wait, Pyeon Yejun's only 18.

636
00:28:21.733 --> 00:28:23.535
Geez, he's 18?

637
00:28:24.870 --> 00:28:27.973
When I was 18,
I had my very first 4-round fight.

638
00:28:28.040 --> 00:28:29.708
- For real?
- Really?

639
00:28:30.275 --> 00:28:32.377
- Pyeon Yejun's got strong momentum.
- Right.

640
00:28:32.444 --> 00:28:33.879
He's small, but strong.

641
00:28:34.479 --> 00:28:36.181
But last time I watched Cho Hyunjae,

642
00:28:36.248 --> 00:28:37.983
I noticed he fights like an out-boxer.

643
00:28:38.050 --> 00:28:40.219
- Yes, that's right.
- Really stylish.

644
00:28:40.285 --> 00:28:42.354
He's super fast.

645
00:28:43.055 --> 00:28:45.023
Their styles are totally different,

646
00:28:45.090 --> 00:28:46.959
so it'll be fun to watch.

647
00:28:47.025 --> 00:28:48.093
Let's begin.

648
00:28:48.694 --> 00:28:50.996
Let's go!

649
00:28:51.063 --> 00:28:53.432
{\an8}KAFAC BOXER CHO HYUNJAE
VS 18-YEAR-OLD MMA FIGHTER PYEON YEJUN

650
00:28:53.498 --> 00:28:54.700
{\an8}Let's go, Pyeon Yejun!

651
00:28:54.766 --> 00:28:55.767
Box!

652
00:28:55.834 --> 00:28:57.636
Box!

653
00:28:57.703 --> 00:28:59.204
{\an8}- Close the distance. Step in!
- Go!

654
00:28:59.271 --> 00:29:00.839
{\an8}- That's it!
- Get in there!

655
00:29:00.906 --> 00:29:02.174
{\an8}HYUNJAE X YEJUN

656
00:29:06.812 --> 00:29:08.547
- There you go!
- All right!

657
00:29:08.614 --> 00:29:09.848
- You're doing great!
- Nice!

658
00:29:09.915 --> 00:29:11.917
Pyeon Yejun's coming on strong.

659
00:29:11.984 --> 00:29:12.985
All right!

660
00:29:14.486 --> 00:29:16.421
- Nice one!
- He caught him.

661
00:29:16.488 --> 00:29:18.890
It's all about timing!
Keep your rhythm!

662
00:29:20.158 --> 00:29:22.294
Throw the lead first! Great!

663
00:29:25.130 --> 00:29:26.298
Nice!

664
00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:29.067
I got a little momentum early on,

665
00:29:29.635 --> 00:29:31.903
so all I was thinking
about was getting a KO.

666
00:29:32.838 --> 00:29:34.573
Yejun, you're doing great!

667
00:29:35.040 --> 00:29:36.208
Just fire away!

668
00:29:36.275 --> 00:29:37.276
The head. That's it.

669
00:29:37.342 --> 00:29:39.144
No... Oh, nice! Nice dodge.

670
00:29:39.211 --> 00:29:41.613
Wow, he's reading him well.

671
00:29:42.381 --> 00:29:43.882
Go for the body first!

672
00:29:45.250 --> 00:29:46.985
- All right!
- Keep those feet moving.

673
00:29:47.052 --> 00:29:49.588
- Stack up those points!
- Nice uppercut!

674
00:29:50.455 --> 00:29:52.424
All right! Nice shot!

675
00:29:52.491 --> 00:29:54.693
- Looks like he'll win this.
- That Pyeon Yejun kid.

676
00:29:54.760 --> 00:29:56.695
He's something else, isn't he?

677
00:29:57.796 --> 00:30:00.399
His punches early on
had this unusual trajectory.

678
00:30:00.465 --> 00:30:03.101
They came in slow,
out of my field of vision.

679
00:30:03.168 --> 00:30:05.437
It threw me off a bit.

680
00:30:06.204 --> 00:30:07.439
Hyunjae, your distance!

681
00:30:07.506 --> 00:30:09.975
- Close the distance!
- Keep it short!

682
00:30:10.042 --> 00:30:11.943
Hyunjae, just loosen up!

683
00:30:12.010 --> 00:30:13.278
There! Good!

684
00:30:13.779 --> 00:30:14.780
Just let it go!

685
00:30:15.280 --> 00:30:16.581
I tried to find my rhythm,

686
00:30:16.648 --> 00:30:19.851
and loosen up by circling around the ring.

687
00:30:24.356 --> 00:30:26.191
Yes, use the jab. That's it.

688
00:30:27.726 --> 00:30:29.828
All right, nice lead hand!

689
00:30:29.895 --> 00:30:31.797
Throw a feint, a feint!

690
00:30:31.863 --> 00:30:32.864
That's it!

691
00:30:34.533 --> 00:30:35.967
- There you go.
- Nice footwork.

692
00:30:36.034 --> 00:30:37.302
- All right.
- He's got to step in.

693
00:30:37.369 --> 00:30:38.403
Nice speed!

694
00:30:39.271 --> 00:30:40.772
- All right!
- Nice shot!

695
00:30:40.839 --> 00:30:43.575
Hyunjae, you're getting into your rhythm!

696
00:30:43.642 --> 00:30:45.477
Hyunjae's footwork is waking up now.

697
00:30:46.011 --> 00:30:48.880
{\an8}Punch then guard!
Punch then guard!

698
00:30:48.947 --> 00:30:50.982
{\an8}- All right, doing good!
- That's it!

699
00:30:51.850 --> 00:30:53.452
{\an8}- There you go!
- Nice one!

700
00:30:57.022 --> 00:30:59.191
{\an8}Okay, time!

701
00:30:59.257 --> 00:31:00.292
{\an8}Yejun, you're a beast!

702
00:31:00.359 --> 00:31:02.561
You did awesome!

703
00:31:03.795 --> 00:31:05.931
- He looks a little tense.
- He does.

704
00:31:05.997 --> 00:31:08.900
I think he's just not warmed up yet.

705
00:31:08.967 --> 00:31:11.636
Early on, he got caught by a punch
he didn't see coming.

706
00:31:11.703 --> 00:31:12.771
That looping hook.

707
00:31:12.838 --> 00:31:16.441
When you get hit by something like that,
it stuns you for a second.

708
00:31:17.142 --> 00:31:19.778
Most boxers go into their usual pattern
out of habit.

709
00:31:19.845 --> 00:31:23.048
They open with that standard pattern.
"Bam, bam, bam."

710
00:31:23.115 --> 00:31:25.050
He was probably expecting that, but then...

711
00:31:25.117 --> 00:31:27.185
That looping shot came out of nowhere.

712
00:31:27.252 --> 00:31:28.687
It must've rattled him early on.

713
00:31:28.754 --> 00:31:30.122
He certainly seemed stunned.

714
00:31:30.188 --> 00:31:32.557
- But still, he pulled himself together.
- Mmm.

715
00:31:32.624 --> 00:31:35.360
Cho Hyunjae was a little shaken
in the beginning,

716
00:31:35.427 --> 00:31:38.363
but as time went on,
he started finding his pace again.

717
00:31:38.430 --> 00:31:40.031
That wasn't completely one-sided.

718
00:31:40.098 --> 00:31:42.467
My shots were landing one after another,

719
00:31:42.534 --> 00:31:45.404
so I thought it'd be an easier fight
than expected.

720
00:31:45.971 --> 00:31:47.639
You're the man!

721
00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:50.842
He's famous for that.

722
00:31:59.351 --> 00:32:00.819
All right, nice!

723
00:32:00.886 --> 00:32:02.621
- Do whatever you want!
- Great!

724
00:32:05.590 --> 00:32:08.326
Hyunjae, the body's open on the left.

725
00:32:08.393 --> 00:32:09.895
Last round! Stay focused!

726
00:32:09.961 --> 00:32:11.096
Keep it together!

727
00:32:13.331 --> 00:32:15.267
- Yejun, breathe!
- Deep breaths!

728
00:32:15.333 --> 00:32:16.968
Loosen up when you throw!

729
00:32:17.035 --> 00:32:19.638
Just do your thing!
Stick to your style!

730
00:32:20.906 --> 00:32:22.073
{\an8}Let's go, Hyunjae!

731
00:32:22.140 --> 00:32:24.342
{\an8}Last one, last round!

732
00:32:24.409 --> 00:32:26.778
{\an8}- Let's go!
- Let's go!

733
00:32:26.845 --> 00:32:28.580
{\an8}HYUNJAE X YEJUN

734
00:32:29.414 --> 00:32:30.549
That's it!

735
00:32:30.615 --> 00:32:32.117
One more, one more!

736
00:32:32.184 --> 00:32:33.185
That's it!

737
00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.421
Uppercut incoming!

738
00:32:36.488 --> 00:32:39.791
- He's finally loosened up.
- There you go! All right!

739
00:32:40.692 --> 00:32:41.893
One more! Bam!

740
00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:43.061
Go again!

741
00:32:43.128 --> 00:32:44.729
- All right!
- Drive it in!

742
00:32:44.796 --> 00:32:45.997
All right!

743
00:32:46.064 --> 00:32:47.065
Drive it in!

744
00:32:47.132 --> 00:32:48.633
- Nice, doing good!
- That's it!

745
00:32:49.267 --> 00:32:52.671
Cho Hyunjae's footwork
got pretty aggressive.

746
00:32:52.737 --> 00:32:54.005
He came in pretty hard.

747
00:32:54.873 --> 00:32:56.374
If you want to slow down his feet,

748
00:32:56.441 --> 00:32:57.876
you need to do some damage.

749
00:32:57.943 --> 00:32:59.177
You gotta get rough with it!

750
00:32:59.244 --> 00:33:00.245
Rough it up, man!

751
00:33:01.813 --> 00:33:03.181
- You got this!
- Let's go!

752
00:33:03.248 --> 00:33:04.749
All right!

753
00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:07.652
- That's it!
- He's caught!

754
00:33:07.719 --> 00:33:09.120
Get in there!

755
00:33:09.588 --> 00:33:11.056
All right!

756
00:33:11.122 --> 00:33:13.558
I saw Pyeon Yejun's hair whip back,

757
00:33:14.059 --> 00:33:16.127
and that's when I thought,

758
00:33:16.194 --> 00:33:17.696
"Round 2 is all mine now."

759
00:33:19.164 --> 00:33:20.365
Hyunjae's too fast.

760
00:33:20.432 --> 00:33:22.167
- Yeah?
- His counters. Yes.

761
00:33:23.568 --> 00:33:24.569
Nice!

762
00:33:30.642 --> 00:33:32.310
He needs to step in.

763
00:33:34.946 --> 00:33:36.181
That's it!

764
00:33:37.649 --> 00:33:38.984
Good counter there!

765
00:33:39.050 --> 00:33:40.118
That's it!

766
00:33:40.185 --> 00:33:41.620
Feint and fire!

767
00:33:41.686 --> 00:33:42.787
All right!

768
00:33:43.455 --> 00:33:45.390
