00:56:19.576 --> 00:56:21.111
{\an8}Stop!

1268
00:56:21.778 --> 00:56:23.480
- Well, that was...
- He won way too easily.

1269
00:56:23.547 --> 00:56:25.782
He breezed through it.

1270
00:56:25.849 --> 00:56:28.452
- Man, he's good.
- These amateurs...

1271
00:56:28.518 --> 00:56:29.853
Their style freaks me out.

1272
00:56:29.920 --> 00:56:31.255
Man, Lee Chaehyun

1273
00:56:31.321 --> 00:56:34.191
- showed us what boxing really is.
- That was real boxing.

1274
00:56:34.258 --> 00:56:36.760
Boxing isn't a brawl. It's a sport.

1275
00:56:37.694 --> 00:56:40.230
We'll announce the decision now.

1276
00:56:40.297 --> 00:56:42.599
The survivor of this deathmatch is...

1277
00:56:43.166 --> 00:56:44.401
{\an8}Lee Chaehyun.

1278
00:56:44.468 --> 00:56:46.436
{\an8}BLUE CORNER LEE CHAEHYUN SURVIVES

1279
00:56:46.904 --> 00:56:48.238
- Well played.
- Good game.

1280
00:56:48.305 --> 00:56:49.940
- Congratulations.
- You both did so well,

1281
00:56:50.007 --> 00:56:51.842
fighting your hearts out.

1282
00:56:51.909 --> 00:56:52.910
He's so cool.

1283
00:56:52.976 --> 00:56:55.045
Lee Chaehyun's on another level.

1284
00:56:55.112 --> 00:56:56.446
He's just too good.

1285
00:56:56.847 --> 00:56:57.848
First off,

1286
00:56:58.548 --> 00:57:00.317
I'm really glad that I got the win.

1287
00:57:00.884 --> 00:57:02.686
I'll keep working hard

1288
00:57:02.753 --> 00:57:04.187
to climb even higher.

1289
00:57:08.558 --> 00:57:11.929
I lost the first fight
and got back in through the extra pass.

1290
00:57:11.995 --> 00:57:14.665
And you gave me
another huge chance this time,

1291
00:57:14.731 --> 00:57:17.401
but I still couldn't make the most of it.

1292
00:57:17.801 --> 00:57:19.870
I'm really mad at myself for that.

1293
00:57:19.937 --> 00:57:23.407
I promised my wife
I'd take her to Las Vegas.

1294
00:57:23.473 --> 00:57:25.742
I'll just take her somewhere even better.

1295
00:57:25.809 --> 00:57:27.411
- I love you, Jihyun.
- You're the man!

1296
00:57:29.947 --> 00:57:31.315
I'd better do that too.

1297
00:57:31.381 --> 00:57:32.983
- You're the man!
- You did awesome!

1298
00:57:35.819 --> 00:57:38.522
{\an8}POST-MATCH BREAK

1299
00:57:41.892 --> 00:57:44.294
Hey, you're like a bull.

1300
00:57:53.370 --> 00:57:55.439
It's making you itch to fight, huh?

1301
00:57:56.606 --> 00:57:59.276
I've learned a lot in theory.
Like, the shoulder should go...

1302
00:57:59.676 --> 00:58:01.178
Right. When you punch?

1303
00:58:01.244 --> 00:58:02.713
But I can't do it in practice.

1304
00:58:02.779 --> 00:58:04.181
You need to put in some work.

1305
00:58:04.247 --> 00:58:05.549
Yeah, that's it!

1306
00:58:05.615 --> 00:58:07.951
- It takes a lot of practice.
- It's tough.

1307
00:58:08.018 --> 00:58:09.219
It's really hard.

1308
00:58:10.053 --> 00:58:11.054
It's the shoulder pop.

1309
00:58:11.555 --> 00:58:13.123
You don't even need to swing big.

1310
00:58:13.190 --> 00:58:14.591
Your shoulder just snaps naturally.

1311
00:58:16.326 --> 00:58:17.995
You gotta pick it up over the years.

1312
00:58:18.061 --> 00:58:20.564
- Yeah, like that.
- You have to pop it.

1313
00:58:20.630 --> 00:58:23.467
It's something I can't teach you how.

1314
00:58:23.533 --> 00:58:25.736
I don't understand the mechanics of it.

1315
00:58:26.837 --> 00:58:31.875
Let's continue with the next matchup
of <i>I Am Boxer's</i> deathmatch.

1316
00:58:31.942 --> 00:58:33.610
The lineup's still stacked.

1317
00:58:34.244 --> 00:58:35.979
- Man, I'm losing my mind.
- It's nerve-racking.

1318
00:58:36.046 --> 00:58:37.647
I'm losing my mind.

1319
00:58:38.215 --> 00:58:39.883
Most eliminated fighters are strong.

1320
00:58:39.950 --> 00:58:41.718
Right.

1321
00:58:41.785 --> 00:58:44.354
<i>I hope none of them come back.</i>

1322
00:58:44.421 --> 00:58:47.024
If they come back,
I'll have to fight them again.

1323
00:58:50.794 --> 00:58:53.330
The fighter to enter the deathmatch is...

1324
00:58:58.235 --> 00:58:59.603
Kim Taesun.

1325
00:59:00.437 --> 00:59:01.805
Kim Taesun.

1326
00:59:04.374 --> 00:59:05.976
I knew it.

1327
00:59:06.043 --> 00:59:07.978
The resurrected prince.

1328
00:59:08.045 --> 00:59:09.379
Always coming back, like a phoenix.

1329
00:59:09.446 --> 00:59:11.481
He should change his nickname to that.

1330
00:59:11.982 --> 00:59:13.417
- Look at how happy he is.
- I know.

1331
00:59:13.483 --> 00:59:14.551
Lucky guy.

1332
00:59:15.118 --> 00:59:18.355
And the fighter facing Kim Taesun is...

1333
00:59:19.256 --> 00:59:20.424
Who's it gonna be?

1334
00:59:20.924 --> 00:59:22.225
A rematch?

1335
00:59:23.760 --> 00:59:24.861
Oh, Kim Minuk?

1336
00:59:26.029 --> 00:59:28.865
<i>I had a feeling I might go up
against Kim Taesun one more time.</i>

1337
00:59:31.835 --> 00:59:34.604
Kim Minuk!

1338
00:59:35.405 --> 00:59:38.008
Wow, round two!

1339
00:59:38.075 --> 00:59:39.443
It's a rematch!

1340
00:59:40.410 --> 00:59:43.880
That's brutal!

1341
00:59:51.888 --> 00:59:52.956
Honored, sir.

1342
00:59:53.023 --> 00:59:54.324
We've got a rematch, everyone.

1343
00:59:54.391 --> 00:59:57.194
KIM MINUK VS KIM TAESUN

1344
00:59:57.260 --> 00:59:59.663
Taesun kept saying
he wanted to fight him again.

1345
01:00:00.564 --> 01:00:02.666
Finally, it's happening.

1346
01:00:03.166 --> 01:00:07.270
Well, he beat me once, after all.

1347
01:00:08.205 --> 01:00:10.307
Hey, get out of there.

1348
01:00:10.373 --> 01:00:12.008
He puts weight behind each one.

1349
01:00:12.476 --> 01:00:13.944
You can see the precision.

1350
01:00:15.745 --> 01:00:17.447
The winner of this match is...

1351
01:00:17.514 --> 01:00:18.815
Kim Minuk from the red corner.

1352
01:00:20.684 --> 01:00:23.520
<i>It was seriously devastating.</i>

1353
01:00:23.587 --> 01:00:26.223
I never want to lose to him again.

1354
01:00:27.357 --> 01:00:28.758
Looking forward to this.

1355
01:00:29.226 --> 01:00:30.227
I'll prove it

1356
01:00:30.994 --> 01:00:32.429
with my real skills.

1357
01:00:34.831 --> 01:00:36.066
He seems really serious.

1358
01:00:36.900 --> 01:00:40.504
Kim Taesun's usually the playful type,

1359
01:00:40.570 --> 01:00:42.405
but he's dead serious right now.

1360
01:00:42.472 --> 01:00:44.074
If he wins this,

1361
01:00:44.608 --> 01:00:45.976
he's a real phoenix.

1362
01:00:46.042 --> 01:00:48.345
Beating the guy he already lost to once.

1363
01:00:48.778 --> 01:00:51.481
I'll put in the effort
and make it through again. Thank you.

1364
01:00:52.883 --> 01:00:54.151
Since he's beaten him before,

1365
01:00:54.217 --> 01:00:56.019
I think he'll fight the way he did then.

1366
01:00:56.086 --> 01:00:58.555
Kim Minuk looks confident.

1367
01:00:59.022 --> 01:01:00.690
He's got that signature calmness.

1368
01:01:01.892 --> 01:01:03.793
This match has two rounds after all.

1369
01:01:03.860 --> 01:01:05.662
- Yeah. You're right.
- Anything can happen.

1370
01:01:05.729 --> 01:01:07.464
And last time,

1371
01:01:08.031 --> 01:01:11.067
Kim Taesun poured everything out

1372
01:01:11.134 --> 01:01:12.469
- and still lost.
- Right.

1373
01:01:12.536 --> 01:01:14.838
- So how's he gonna approach it this time?
- Yes.

1374
01:01:14.905 --> 01:01:16.973
- Exactly.
- Yes, that's the key.

1375
01:01:19.543 --> 01:01:21.811
- If he changes it up, that means...
- Right.

1376
01:01:21.878 --> 01:01:24.481
...he learned something from the experience.

1377
01:01:24.548 --> 01:01:26.016
That'll be interesting to see.

1378
01:01:27.417 --> 01:01:29.586
I'm really curious how this will play out.

1379
01:01:30.520 --> 01:01:31.688
<i>I was confident.</i>

1380
01:01:32.255 --> 01:01:33.823
<i>There's nowhere left to run,</i>

1381
01:01:33.890 --> 01:01:36.159
<i>so I'll just have to step over him
and climb back up.</i>

1382
01:01:37.360 --> 01:01:40.530
<i>If I lose again...
Even the thought of it is terrifying.</i>

1383
01:01:40.597 --> 01:01:42.532
<i>I have to win this time.</i>

1384
01:01:44.935 --> 01:01:46.303
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1385
01:01:46.369 --> 01:01:48.338
{\an8}FORMER ASIAN SUPER LIGHTWEIGHT CHAMP
KIM MINUK

1386
01:01:48.972 --> 01:01:50.073
{\an8}Let's do this!

1387
01:01:50.774 --> 01:01:52.309
- This one's going to be fun.
- Totally.

1388
01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:53.376
Box!

1389
01:01:54.744 --> 01:01:57.013
{\an8}- All right!
- You got this!

1390
01:01:57.080 --> 01:02:01.551
{\an8}MINUK X TAESUN

1391
01:02:01.618 --> 01:02:02.919
They're sizing each other up.

1392
01:02:05.422 --> 01:02:06.690
His jab's just...

1393
01:02:06.756 --> 01:02:07.924
It's heavy.

1394
01:02:09.659 --> 01:02:10.660
Nice stance.

1395
01:02:10.727 --> 01:02:12.562
- He's gotta go first. That's it.
- That's it.

1396
01:02:12.629 --> 01:02:13.763
This is tense.

1397
01:02:13.830 --> 01:02:15.832
My palms are sweating.

1398
01:02:18.835 --> 01:02:19.836
- Nice body shot!
- There!

1399
01:02:19.903 --> 01:02:20.971
Nice body shot.

1400
01:02:21.638 --> 01:02:23.707
Love how relaxed he is.

1401
01:02:27.244 --> 01:02:28.845
His rhythm's completely different.

1402
01:02:28.912 --> 01:02:31.348
- From last time?
- He's a lot more careful.

1403
01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:32.749
He shouldn't be scared, though.

1404
01:02:33.416 --> 01:02:35.151
Play the offense, the offense.

1405
01:02:38.288 --> 01:02:39.556
He's moving slow today.

1406
01:02:39.623 --> 01:02:40.991
Got to go in first, man.

1407
01:02:42.692 --> 01:02:44.361
Wait, he's not usually like this.

1408
01:02:45.061 --> 01:02:47.364
- Taesun looks a little intimidated.
- Right?

1409
01:02:47.430 --> 01:02:49.099
Taesun seems really tense.

1410
01:02:49.666 --> 01:02:52.769
I usually fight with more energy,

1411
01:02:52.836 --> 01:02:55.272
but I couldn't help feeling
the pressure today.

1412
01:02:56.306 --> 01:02:58.008
<i>"If I lose again, I'm done for."</i>

1413
01:02:58.074 --> 01:03:00.143
<i>"What if Plan A doesn't work?"</i>

1414
01:03:00.210 --> 01:03:01.811
<i>"What's my Plan B?"</i>

1415
01:03:01.878 --> 01:03:05.148
<i>Thoughts like that kept swirling,</i>

1416
01:03:05.215 --> 01:03:06.883
and I got pushed back early on.

1417
01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:09.886
Nice!

1418
01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:12.122
- That's it!
- He's got it.

1419
01:03:15.992 --> 01:03:17.294
They landed at the same time.

1420
01:03:17.994 --> 01:03:20.397
- Swing with confidence. Nice.
- Come on, swing first!

1421
01:03:21.631 --> 01:03:22.732
Nice, keep up the footwork.

1422
01:03:25.201 --> 01:03:26.603
- He's cornered.
- That's it.

1423
01:03:26.670 --> 01:03:28.071
- Go, go!
- Okay, now go for it.

1424
01:03:28.138 --> 01:03:29.205
Go for it!

1425
01:03:29.272 --> 01:03:30.674
- Go! This is it!
- Go!

1426
01:03:35.578 --> 01:03:36.713
Oh!

1427
01:03:36.780 --> 01:03:38.481
How is he landing that from there?

1428
01:03:39.149 --> 01:03:41.117
Watch out for the right uppercut!

1429
01:03:46.122 --> 01:03:48.191
He's tracking his movement.

1430
01:03:48.958 --> 01:03:51.361
This range actually favors Minuk.

1431
01:03:54.898 --> 01:03:57.434
<i>I can inflict more damage
when I'm backed into the ropes,</i>

1432
01:03:57.500 --> 01:03:59.769
<i>so I signaled for Kim Taesun
to come in, but he didn't.</i>

1433
01:04:02.972 --> 01:04:04.808
"Fine, I'll go then."

1434
01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:11.815
I love cheeky stuff like this.

1435
01:04:13.717 --> 01:04:14.984
Damn, nice angle.

1436
01:04:15.051 --> 01:04:16.886
Kim Minuk's got the flow on his side.

1437
01:04:19.522 --> 01:04:21.524
- Ten seconds!
- Round 1 is over.

1438
01:04:21.591 --> 01:04:23.593
- They didn't spend much energy.
- A lead uppercut!

1439
01:04:27.864 --> 01:04:32.102
{\an8}MINUK X TAESUN

1440
01:04:35.705 --> 01:04:37.307
That connected hard.

1441
01:04:37.374 --> 01:04:38.575
Nice! Now, rush him!

1442
01:04:39.376 --> 01:04:40.377
That's it!

1443
01:04:42.946 --> 01:04:45.382
{\an8}MINUK X TAESUN

1444
01:04:51.287 --> 01:04:52.288
Nice one!

1445
01:04:52.355 --> 01:04:54.224
- Way to go!
- That was a great rush!

1446
01:04:54.290 --> 01:04:56.259
- You're loosening up!
- You got this!

1447
01:04:56.760 --> 01:04:59.195
- He landed that combo. Bam!
- And that straight. Bam!

1448
01:04:59.262 --> 01:05:01.731
- It's a whole different fight this time.
- Holy cow.

1449
01:05:01.798 --> 01:05:04.467
He was dominating,
until those two shots landed at the end.

1450
01:05:04.534 --> 01:05:06.669
- He let his guard down.
- That's what it looked like.

1451
01:05:07.170 --> 01:05:09.005
Minuk staggered a bit there.

1452
01:05:09.072 --> 01:05:11.040
That last shot really caught him clean.

1453
01:05:11.107 --> 01:05:13.309
Ten more seconds,
who knows what would've happened?

1454
01:05:13.376 --> 01:05:14.644
That was dangerous.

1455
01:05:14.711 --> 01:05:18.281
At the end of Round 1,
I lost my balance for a second

1456
01:05:18.348 --> 01:05:20.250
and took two solid shots.

1457
01:05:23.953 --> 01:05:28.091
That definitely drained my stamina.
Those hits.

1458
01:05:28.158 --> 01:05:29.859
He looks a bit worn out.

1459
01:05:30.760 --> 01:05:33.096
<i>I thought, "This is going good."</i>

1460
01:05:33.163 --> 01:05:34.564
Let's go, Kim Taesun!

1461
01:05:34.631 --> 01:05:35.765
Stay cool!

1462
01:05:37.000 --> 01:05:39.469
- Let's go!
- Come on!

1463
01:05:39.536 --> 01:05:41.304
- You got this!
- Keep it up!

1464
01:05:41.371 --> 01:05:42.972
- Good going!
- Let's move up again!

1465
01:05:43.540 --> 01:05:45.108
He has to step it up this round.

1466
01:05:45.175 --> 01:05:46.709
Well, he's a natural competitor.

1467
01:05:46.776 --> 01:05:49.012
- He's gotta be aggressive now.
- This is gonna be intense.

1468
01:05:49.078 --> 01:05:50.980
I know. Round 2 is gonna be fire.

1469
01:05:51.047 --> 01:05:52.682
- You never know with boxing.
- Exactly.

1470
01:05:52.749 --> 01:05:54.484
We'll have to see
how this round plays out.

1471
01:06:03.426 --> 01:06:04.427
{\an8}MINUK X TAESUN

1472
01:06:05.562 --> 01:06:07.530
{\an8}- Let's go, Taesun!
- Let's do this!

1473
01:06:08.832 --> 01:06:10.667
{\an8}Feels like the real fight's starting now.

1474
01:06:11.935 --> 01:06:13.069
{\an8}Feints, feints!

1475
01:06:14.304 --> 01:06:15.305
That's it!

1476
01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:17.373
Move! Gotta keep moving!

1477
01:06:17.440 --> 01:06:19.642
- He looks a bit pissed.
- Yeah, he does.

1478
01:06:19.709 --> 01:06:21.311
- He'll start pressuring now.
- Yeah.

1479
01:06:22.011 --> 01:06:23.880
Minuk's kind of like a lion.

1480
01:06:23.947 --> 01:06:25.114
He's got that presence.

1481
01:06:25.782 --> 01:06:26.950
Yeah!

1482
01:06:27.016 --> 01:06:29.519
Come on, one for one! All right, nice!

1483
01:06:29.586 --> 01:06:31.187
His speed's on another level.

1484
01:06:35.191 --> 01:06:37.760
There's that snap in Minuk's punches.

1485
01:06:38.228 --> 01:06:39.262
Stay calm.

1486
01:06:39.329 --> 01:06:40.897
It's not over yet. Stay sharp!

1487
01:06:48.671 --> 01:06:50.240
That's it!

1488
01:06:50.306 --> 01:06:51.774
They're both landing shots now.

1489
01:06:52.876 --> 01:06:54.577
Keep moving! Keep moving!

1490
01:06:54.644 --> 01:06:56.179
Taesun, hit and then move!

1491
01:06:57.280 --> 01:06:59.849
<i>I'm known as a power puncher,</i>

1492
01:06:59.916 --> 01:07:02.285
<i>but my reach is one of my biggest weapons.</i>

1493
01:07:02.952 --> 01:07:06.256
<i>This time, I tried to use that advantage</i>

1494
01:07:06.322 --> 01:07:10.159
<i>and fought from
the longest range possible.</i>

1495
01:07:13.096 --> 01:07:14.697
Taesun, slip in a quick shot!

1496
01:07:17.033 --> 01:07:18.368
Nice left shot!

1497
01:07:21.337 --> 01:07:22.739
Taesun avoids shots well.

1498
01:07:22.805 --> 01:07:24.374
He covers well too.

1499
01:07:24.440 --> 01:07:26.009
All right!

1500
01:07:26.075 --> 01:07:27.844
There you go, counter punch!

1501
01:07:31.080 --> 01:07:32.515
Go again, jab lightly.

1502
01:07:33.283 --> 01:07:34.450
Wait, he's done a 180.

1503
01:07:34.517 --> 01:07:35.952
Keep it loose!

1504
01:07:36.586 --> 01:07:39.155
- His strategy's a bit different now.
- This is Round 2.

1505
01:07:42.125 --> 01:07:43.459
His punches look weaker now.

1506
01:07:43.526 --> 01:07:45.495
- Relax.
- He's just standing still.

1507
01:07:49.599 --> 01:07:50.600
Break!

1508
01:07:51.267 --> 01:07:52.869
No, you've got to keep throwing.

1509
01:07:52.936 --> 01:07:55.004
Oh, man. He's gassed.

1510
01:07:55.505 --> 01:07:56.606
His stamina's dropping.

1511
01:07:57.340 --> 01:07:58.641
{\an8}MINUK X TAESUN

1512
01:07:58.708 --> 01:08:00.109
{\an8}- Ten seconds left.
- Ten seconds!

1513
01:08:03.813 --> 01:08:05.682
Okay, that's it!

1514
01:08:06.516 --> 01:08:08.351
Empty the tank! Final push!

1515
01:08:09.018 --> 01:08:10.787
- Pour it all out!
- Let's go!

1516
01:08:10.853 --> 01:08:11.854
Pour it all out!

1517
01:08:11.921 --> 01:08:13.122
- Ten seconds!
- Ten seconds!

1518
01:08:15.358 --> 01:08:16.826
Stop!

1519
01:08:17.794 --> 01:08:19.028
All right!

1520
01:08:20.463 --> 01:08:22.465
Wow, that was insane.

1521
01:08:24.667 --> 01:08:26.769
- Taesun did pretty well, though.
- Yeah.

1522
01:08:26.836 --> 01:08:29.606
- He held his own.
- He fought way better than last time.

1523
01:08:29.672 --> 01:08:31.641
He may be older now,
but he's still got it.

1524
01:08:31.708 --> 01:08:33.910
Minuk doesn't even compete anymore.

1525
01:08:33.977 --> 01:08:35.411
Man, that was a great fight.

1526
01:08:35.478 --> 01:08:37.380
- This was so fun.
- Way more fun than expected.

1527
01:08:37.447 --> 01:08:39.482
- It was way more fun.
- It was awesome.

1528
01:08:39.549 --> 01:08:41.551
All right, we'll announce the decision

1529
01:08:42.318 --> 01:08:43.453
right now.

1530
01:08:46.422 --> 01:08:48.257
How do you even call this?

1531
01:08:48.324 --> 01:08:51.427
Red landed more clean shots overall,

1532
01:08:51.494 --> 01:08:54.063
but that last punch
from blue really connected.

1533
01:08:54.130 --> 01:08:55.198
That was huge.

1534
01:08:55.264 --> 01:08:58.534
As for Round 2, I think

1535
01:08:58.601 --> 01:09:00.470
Kim Taesun landed more effective shots.

1536
01:09:00.536 --> 01:09:03.640
I think blue will win.
He landed more punches.

1537
01:09:03.706 --> 01:09:06.576
Judge one scores it for...

1538
01:09:06.643 --> 01:09:08.244
Can't wait to hear this.

1539
01:09:10.546 --> 01:09:11.881
{\an8}Kim Taesun from the blue corner!

1540
01:09:11.948 --> 01:09:13.583
{\an8}- Kim Taesun from the blue corner!
- Yes!

1541
01:09:16.653 --> 01:09:17.654
All right!

1542
01:09:17.720 --> 01:09:19.689
Judge two scores it for...

1543
01:09:21.824 --> 01:09:23.860
<i>I honestly thought I had it.</i>

1544
01:09:25.695 --> 01:09:28.064
<i>I've been eliminated twice already.</i>

1545
01:09:28.564 --> 01:09:30.433
<i>I really wanted to win.</i>

1546
01:09:31.934 --> 01:09:33.936
Judge two scores it for...

1547
01:09:36.372 --> 01:09:38.408
{\an8}Kim Taesun from the blue corner!

1548
01:09:38.875 --> 01:09:40.476
{\an8}Kim Taesun from the blue corner!

1549
01:09:42.045 --> 01:09:45.748
By unanimous decision,
the survivor of this deathmatch

1550
01:09:45.815 --> 01:09:46.883
is Kim Taesun.

1551
01:09:46.949 --> 01:09:48.217
{\an8}Thank you very much!

1552
01:09:48.284 --> 01:09:49.519
{\an8}BLUE CORNER KIM TAESUN SURVIVES

1553
01:09:49.585 --> 01:09:51.454
{\an8}Wow, he got his revenge.

1554
01:09:51.521 --> 01:09:52.722
He's incredible.

1555
01:09:53.156 --> 01:09:54.290
Our phoenix!

1556
01:09:55.291 --> 01:09:56.826
- He survived this.
- He actually did.

1557
01:09:56.893 --> 01:09:58.294
- He keeps coming back.
- He did it.

1558
01:09:59.562 --> 01:10:01.431
<i>"I've still got it," I thought.</i>

1559
01:10:01.497 --> 01:10:03.166
<i>Life's about grinding your way up.</i>

1560
01:10:03.800 --> 01:10:05.535
So grind I will.

1561
01:10:07.170 --> 01:10:09.672
Now, these two
must've sparked the question

1562
01:10:09.739 --> 01:10:11.974
"Who'd win if they squared off?"

1563
01:10:12.041 --> 01:10:16.112
I'm sure the viewers have been
waiting for this matchup.

1564
01:10:16.879 --> 01:10:19.215
The fighter to enter the deathmatch is...

1565
01:10:20.316 --> 01:10:21.918
- Who will it be?
- Who will it be?

1566
01:10:23.519 --> 01:10:24.721
Who will it be?

1567
01:10:25.321 --> 01:10:27.156
<i>Whoever survives,
I hope he's not too strong.</i>

1568
01:10:28.391 --> 01:10:29.425
I wonder...

1569
01:10:30.493 --> 01:10:31.627
Myung Hyunman.

1570
01:10:33.196 --> 01:10:35.164
The time has come.

1571
01:10:35.231 --> 01:10:37.333
- Oh, my God.
- Of course it's him.

1572
01:10:37.967 --> 01:10:39.035
Oh!

1573
01:10:39.102 --> 01:10:40.470
Here we go.

1574
01:10:43.940 --> 01:10:45.274
Sheesh.

1575
01:10:46.109 --> 01:10:48.611
- He's huge.
- He's really huge.

1576
01:10:48.678 --> 01:10:52.115
Damn, his physicality is unreal.

1577
01:10:52.181 --> 01:10:54.417
He's built for strength.

1578
01:10:55.051 --> 01:10:57.754
He's a born powerhouse.

1579
01:10:57.820 --> 01:10:58.855
I know.

1580
01:10:59.422 --> 01:11:02.158
You don't see
physicality like that around here.

1581
01:11:02.225 --> 01:11:04.160
I feel intimidated just looking at him.

1582
01:11:04.227 --> 01:11:05.261
I'd be scared.

1583
01:11:05.328 --> 01:11:06.696
Imagine fighting him.

1584
01:11:07.930 --> 01:11:09.732
MYUNG HYUNMAN
FORMER KICKBOXING HEAVYWEIGHT CHAMP

1585
01:11:09.799 --> 01:11:13.970
I don't think there's anyone
who can beat him here.

1586
01:11:14.036 --> 01:11:16.072
Honestly, I could die facing him.

1587
01:11:16.139 --> 01:11:17.740
Are they trying to kill us or what?

1588
01:11:17.807 --> 01:11:19.776
Now this is a literal deathmatch.

1589
01:11:19.842 --> 01:11:23.446
But there's no one in there
who can take him on.

1590
01:11:23.513 --> 01:11:24.981
But you never know up there.

1591
01:11:25.047 --> 01:11:26.315
Everything can flip.

1592
01:11:26.783 --> 01:11:29.685
The fighter facing Myung Hyunman is...

1593
01:11:33.189 --> 01:11:34.857
I think I know who it is.

1594
01:11:35.691 --> 01:11:37.260
I think he knows it too.

1595
01:11:38.227 --> 01:11:40.062
He knows he's the only one
who can face him.

1596
01:11:40.129 --> 01:11:43.166
The fighter facing Myung Hyunman is...

1597
01:11:45.101 --> 01:11:46.302
Julien Kang.

1598
01:11:47.703 --> 01:11:49.172
Man, I knew it.

1599
01:11:53.342 --> 01:11:54.544
This is it!

1600
01:11:54.610 --> 01:11:56.045
Let's go, let's go!

1601
01:11:56.112 --> 01:11:58.047
Wow, look at those shoulders.

1602
01:11:58.114 --> 01:11:59.549
He really is huge.

1603
01:11:59.615 --> 01:12:00.883
He's massive.

1604
01:12:00.950 --> 01:12:02.418
It's like the battle of the giants.

1605
01:12:02.485 --> 01:12:04.020
It's a giant versus a giant.

1606
01:12:04.086 --> 01:12:06.022
Shouldn't there be two referees for this?

1607
01:12:06.088 --> 01:12:07.557
Boy, why am I shaking?

1608
01:12:08.024 --> 01:12:10.126
Feels like a knockout is coming.

1609
01:12:11.260 --> 01:12:12.495
I can't picture it.

1610
01:12:15.164 --> 01:12:16.999
Everyone would definitely
want to see this.

1611
01:12:17.066 --> 01:12:19.669
This is the kind of matchup
you only dream about.

1612
01:12:19.735 --> 01:12:21.671
And now, we actually get to see it.

1613
01:12:22.071 --> 01:12:23.172
{\an8}MYUNG HYUNMAN

1614
01:12:23.239 --> 01:12:25.508
{\an8}Hyunman is about 16 kg heavier,

1615
01:12:26.309 --> 01:12:28.578
{\an8}but Julien has a 12 cm reach advantage.

1616
01:12:28.644 --> 01:12:29.645
{\an8}JULIEN KANG

1617
01:12:29.712 --> 01:12:33.583
That kind of reach gap
is basically bigger than a full fist.

1618
01:12:33.649 --> 01:12:35.885
But with heavyweights, you never know.

1619
01:12:35.952 --> 01:12:38.120
Just as single shot could end everything.

1620
01:12:38.788 --> 01:12:40.122
It can go either way.

1621
01:12:40.189 --> 01:12:41.691
Really can't predict a thing.

1622
01:12:42.158 --> 01:12:44.160
This bout already feels heavier.

1623
01:12:44.227 --> 01:12:46.195
With their weight class and all.

1624
01:12:46.863 --> 01:12:49.365
- I bet there will be a knockdown.
- For sure.

1625
01:12:49.966 --> 01:12:51.767
But with that kind of body,

1626
01:12:51.834 --> 01:12:53.402
Julien Kang won't get hit easily.

1627
01:12:56.138 --> 01:12:59.041
<i>Honestly, I thought
I had a real chance of winning.</i>

1628
01:12:59.108 --> 01:13:01.777
I thought if I just do what I do
in practice every day,

1629
01:13:02.278 --> 01:13:04.347
I could definitely win.

1630
01:13:04.413 --> 01:13:07.316
<i>There's no going back now.</i>

1631
01:13:07.817 --> 01:13:10.553
<i>I have to be the one to move up this time.</i>

1632
01:13:11.087 --> 01:13:14.223
<i>I was like, "Guess I'm going up
against the top celebrity fighter."</i>

1633
01:13:14.757 --> 01:13:17.526
He's got amazing athleticism
and combat instinct,

1634
01:13:17.593 --> 01:13:18.928
but he's not a pro.

1635
01:13:18.995 --> 01:13:21.397
So I thought I'd better
finish him off fast and move on.

1636
01:13:21.864 --> 01:13:24.967
<i>I really felt like I could drop him,
or maybe even KO him.</i>

1637
01:13:25.434 --> 01:13:27.069
My heart's pounding just watching this.

1638
01:13:29.205 --> 01:13:31.941
All right, this is set
to be a fantastic bout.

1639
01:13:32.475 --> 01:13:34.076
Box!

1640
01:13:34.143 --> 01:13:35.711
Let's go!

1641
01:13:35.778 --> 01:13:38.314
{\an8}Let's go!

1642
01:13:38.381 --> 01:13:42.485
{\an8}JULIEN X HYUNMAN

1643
01:13:42.551 --> 01:13:43.886
{\an8}They're treading carefully.

1644
01:13:44.520 --> 01:13:45.655
Throw the jab!

1645
01:13:46.188 --> 01:13:47.290
The jab!

1646
01:13:49.158 --> 01:13:50.626
Break it up!

1647
01:13:52.528 --> 01:13:53.629
Break it up!

1648
01:13:56.098 --> 01:13:57.633
Oh, he got him! He got him.

1649
01:13:58.134 --> 01:14:00.336
Julien Kang's got serious power
behind his shots.

1650
01:14:00.836 --> 01:14:02.071
Damn...

1651
01:14:02.138 --> 01:14:04.540
Julien Kang keeps driving
those long shots in.

1652
01:14:07.877 --> 01:14:08.945
Going for one big shot.

1653
01:14:09.578 --> 01:14:11.414
A punch like that could kill you.

1654
01:14:12.515 --> 01:14:14.784
I think they're pretty evenly--

1655
01:14:14.850 --> 01:14:16.319
He got hit? Whoa!

1656
01:14:31.801 --> 01:14:33.336
Down, down, down!

1657
01:14:33.402 --> 01:14:34.637
He's down!

1658
01:14:36.272 --> 01:14:37.773
<i>I never saw that coming.</i>

1659
01:14:37.840 --> 01:14:39.342
<i>Wow, this is insane.</i>

1660
01:14:39.408 --> 01:14:41.577
<i>Boxing in an arena like that?</i>

1661
01:14:41.644 --> 01:14:43.279
- Wait, what?
- Huh?

1662
01:14:43.346 --> 01:14:44.981
<i>Round 3.</i>

1663
01:14:45.047 --> 01:14:46.415
<i>Three rings.</i>

1664
01:14:46.482 --> 01:14:47.583
<i>I really can't tell.</i>

1665
01:14:54.357 --> 01:14:55.758
<i>This is gonna get real bloody.</i>

1666
01:14:55.825 --> 01:14:56.892
Bring it on!

1667
01:14:56.959 --> 01:14:58.461
He's got to go in.

1668
01:14:59.095 --> 01:15:00.997
- That's it!
- You're almost there!

1669
01:15:01.063 --> 01:15:02.498
You gotta go for it!

1670
01:15:02.565 --> 01:15:03.966
<i>I will survive this.</i>

1671
01:15:27.423 --> 01:15:29.425
Translated by Jisu Park

